{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Use `/etc/inventory/app.conf` on node1 as the source of truth and maintain a matching copy on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A one-way sender on node1 and restricted receiver on node2 were configured. The initial transfer succeeded, and final observations show identical SHA-256 values and root-owned 0644 files on both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a0aa5a437a1740cd","cmd-597905acfd15494d","cmd-19b9d1d21fb144ed","cmd-b992e670d0b448a5","cmd-96a063fd251a4f4d","cmd-2828a2ee4fab415d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Automatically propagate changes from node1 to node2 within 15 minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A synthetic source change was automatically observed on node2 about 13 seconds after the recorded source change, and restoration of the original content also propagated automatically within seconds. The persistent timer remained active after node1 restarted, and node2 received a fresh transfer after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e45d782dc9524169","cmd-15b27078d2d24b35","cmd-176648e096a74197","cmd-c2140e55eddf48e8","cmd-8cba6132d6d74d52","cmd-712d1e8fa1e34458"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution and restarts. The implementation used existing OpenSSH, systemd, Bash, and sudo components; final checks show no added rsync or inotify-tools packages and healthy package-manager state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab51a96e601b446b","cmd-6a07090b1d7b4503","cmd-96a063fd251a4f4d","cmd-2828a2ee4fab415d","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Configuration and account changes directly implemented the synchronization mechanism. The temporary source-content mutation was a bounded behavioral test and was fully restored; no test residue remained. Node restarts were required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Final observations show no failed services, no new listeners, healthy package state, and enforcing SELinux.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a0aa5a437a1740cd","cmd-597905acfd15494d","cmd-19b9d1d21fb144ed","cmd-e45d782dc9524169","cmd-176648e096a74197","cmd-96a063fd251a4f4d","cmd-2828a2ee4fab415d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct change-and-restoration tests demonstrate automatic propagation far inside the 15-minute limit, final source and destination state matches, and the original RHEL release and kernel were retained. The mandatory restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and data, and a successful post-restart transfer.","limitations":["The configuration file was absent on both nodes initially, so there was no pre-existing application content to preserve or compare; the executor necessarily created an empty source and verified synchronization using synthetic content.","Behavioral coverage used one small content change and its restoration rather than an exhaustive range of file sizes or concurrent-update conditions."]}
